          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T14:21:10Z",
          "note": "Testing — T2 toast coverage gap (noted by QA): The mixed credential+non-credential toast branch is exercised implicitly via the DOM badge assertions in the AC4 test, but there is no dedicated assertion on the toast text content for the T2 case. All three toast branches (T1, T2, T3) ideally have explicit message assertions. T1 and T3 are explicitly tested. A T2 assertion would complete the toast coverage triangle. Tagged for consideration in a follow-up test sweep — not blocking."
        },
        {
          "type": "documentation-forward",
          "priority": "medium",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T14:21:10Z",
          "note": "[documentation-forward] workspace-detail.js: The new CREDENTIAL_MISSING_SENTINEL constant, buildMissingCredentialBadge(), applySetupResultCredentialErrors(), and applyStatusMapUpdate() functions are not yet mentioned in the module-level JSDoc block at the top of the file (lines 1–37). The module docstring should be updated to document the credential-error display feature — specifically: (a) the sentinel-based detection mechanism, (b) the amber badge visual distinction from the generic error badge, and (c) the known page-load limitation (badge not shown on reload from prior session). This helps future contributors understand the feature without having to trace through the implementation."
        },
        {
          "type": "documentation-forward",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T14:21:10Z",
          "note": "[documentation-forward] styles.css: The .status-badge-credential rule has a code comment explaining its purpose. Consider adding a brief note in the CSS header or a dedicated section comment grouping all credential-related CSS variables and rules together (currently --badge-credential/--badge-credential-bg appear inline in the badge color block, and the rule appears after .status-badge-error). A grouped comment would make the badge taxonomy clearer to future CSS contributors."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "documentation",
      "status": "IN_PROGRESS",
      "started_at": "2026-06-26T14:21:35Z",
      "summary": []
    }
